  "_comment": "Which configuration values define a composite (#615): accounts whose defining values agree share a composite key, and only they add up to one result. A rule names a path of the rendered document, or a prefix of one; the longest matching rule decides, so a block's rule is the default for every value in it. 'defining' values are part of the key, 'neutral' ones are not, and 'excluding' makes the account an excluded member while it is switched on. The floor is fixed in code and cannot be named here: the run's axes, the resolved account currency, the account model (market_entry.trading_model) and the decision logic (strategy_config.decision_logic_type). Tune it in user_configs/composite_definition.json — every run records the definition it ran under, so a changed definition shows on its keys.",
